  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Word Roller Glitch\n\nA heavy uppercase word swaps with an RGB-split glitch: for eight frames a blue top half and a rose bottom half jitter sideways behind the word, then it holds clean until the next swap.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4.5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- Short, punchy uppercase words (hack, code, ship, win) swapped on a dark title.\n- A cut between words that should read as a signal fault.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The tone is soft or premium: use word-roller-blur.\n- Only one word glitches in once: use rgb-glitch-text or sustained-glitch.\n\nVariables:\n- words (string): Words, default \"HACK, CODE, SHIP, WIN\"\n- prefix (string): Lead-in, default \"READY TO\"\n- font_size (number, 20-320): Font size, default 100\n- color (color): Word color, default \"#fafafa\"\n- prefix_color (color): Lead-in color, default \"#a3a3a3\"\n- glitch_a (color): Glitch top, default \"#38bdf8\"\n- glitch_b (color): Glitch bottom, default \"#f43f5e\"\n- cycle_frames (number, 12-120): Frames per word, default 30\n- background (color): Background, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Word Roller Glitch\n\n  A heavy uppercase word swaps with an RGB-split glitch: for eight frames a blue top half and a rose bottom half jitter sideways behind the word, then it holds clean until the next swap.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes/blob/02c7a84241da7010b5f59c420b0110aafd1d6f0d/src/scenes/RollerAnimations/RollerGlitch.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 lifeprompt-team\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"word-roller-glitch\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"4.5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"words\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Words\", \"description\": \"Words in order, separated by commas. The last one is where it settles.\", \"default\": \"HACK, CODE, SHIP, WIN\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prefix\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Lead-in\", \"description\": \"Small line above the word.\", \"default\": \"READY TO\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Size of the word in pixels. A wide word shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 100, \"min\": 20, \"max\": 320, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Word color\", \"description\": \"Color of the word.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prefix_color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Lead-in color\", \"description\": \"Color of the line above.\", \"default\": \"#a3a3a3\"},\n    {\"id\": \"glitch_a\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Glitch top\", \"description\": \"Color of the top half layer during a glitch.\", \"default\": \"#38bdf8\"},\n    {\"id\": \"glitch_b\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Glitch bottom\", \"description\": \"Color of the bottom half layer during a glitch.\", \"default\": \"#f43f5e\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cycle_frames\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Frames per word\", \"description\": \"How long each word is shown, in 30 fps frames.\", \"default\": 30, \"min\": 12, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"f\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Fill behind the text. Use transparent to lay the block over your own footage.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Word Roller Glitch</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100;300;400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .wgl-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n\n        #root { color: var(--c, #fafafa); }\n        .wgl-g { text-align: center; line-height: 1.1; }\n        .wgl-lead { font-size: 0.24em; font-weight: 400; color: var(--pc, #a3a3a3); margin-bottom: 0.6em; white-space: pre; }\n        .wgl-wrap { position: relative; display: grid; justify-items: center; font-weight: 800; }\n        .wgl-wrap > * { grid-area: 1 / 1; }\n        .wgl-word, .wgl-la, .wgl-lb { font-weight: 800; white-space: pre; }\n        .wgl-word { position: relative; z-index: 1; }\n        .wgl-sizer { grid-area: 1 / 1; }\n        .wgl-la { color: var(--ga, #38bdf8); opacity: 0.9; clip-path: inset(0 0 50% 0); display: none; }\n        .wgl-lb { color: var(--gb, #f43f5e); opacity: 0.9; clip-path: inset(50% 0 0 0); display: none; }\n\n        .wgl-sizer { display: grid; height: 0; overflow: hidden; visibility: hidden; pointer-events: none; }\n        .wgl-sizer span { grid-area: 1 / 1; white-space: pre; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"word-roller-glitch\" data-duration=\"4.5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"wgl-clip\" class=\"wgl-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"4.5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"wgl-g\" class=\"wgl-g\">\n            <div id=\"wgl-lead\" class=\"wgl-lead\"></div>\n            <div class=\"wgl-wrap\">\n              <div id=\"wgl-sizer\" class=\"wgl-sizer\"></div>\n              <div id=\"wgl-la\" class=\"wgl-la\"></div>\n              <div id=\"wgl-lb\" class=\"wgl-lb\"></div>\n              <div id=\"wgl-word\" class=\"wgl-word\"></div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function el(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && value !== undefined && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function txt(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function list(value, fallback, max) {\n              var a = (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n              if (!a.length) a = fallback.slice();\n              return a.slice(0, max || 12);\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            var E = {\n              out: bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), \"in\": bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0), inOut: bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1),\n              overshoot: bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), smooth: bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n              quadIn: function (x) { return x * x; },\n              quadOut: function (x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); },\n              cubicOut: function (x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); },\n              cubicInOut: function (x) { return x < 0.5 ? 4 * x * x * x : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * x + 2, 3) / 2; }\n            };\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            // the source framework interpolate with clamped ends, one input range and one output range.\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 towards 1 (mass, stiffness, damping), frame at 30 fps, in closed form.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness === undefined ? 100 : cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping === undefined ? 10 : cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-6) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              var q = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + q, r2 = -z * w0 - q;\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            // Sets the group's font size, then shrinks it so the group (or its probe) fits the frame.\n            function fitG(g, size, probe, wf, hf, wmul) {\n              g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var p = probe || g;\n              var w = Math.max(1, p.offsetWidth * (wmul || 1)), h = Math.max(1, p.offsetHeight);\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * (wf || 0.9) / w, root.clientHeight * (hf || 0.9) / h);\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(6, size * k); g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function fillSizer(sizer, words) {\n              sizer.textContent = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (w) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.textContent = w;\n                sizer.appendChild(s);\n              });\n            }\n            function setText(node, value) {\n              if (node.__t !== value) { node.__t = value; node.textContent = value; }\n            }\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"4.5\");\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: Math.round(TOTAL * 30), duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(Math.round(clock.frame * speed * 1000) / 1000); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"word-roller-glitch\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            root.style.background = str(vars.background, \"#0a0a0a\");\n            \n            var words = list(vars.words, [\"HACK\", \"CODE\", \"SHIP\", \"WIN\"], 10);\n            var fi = words.length - 1;\n            var cd = num(vars.cycle_frames, 30, 12, 120);\n            var g = el(\"wgl-g\"), lead = el(\"wgl-lead\"), word = el(\"wgl-word\"), la = el(\"wgl-la\"), lb = el(\"wgl-lb\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--c\", vars.color);\n            if (typeof vars.prefix_color === \"string\" && vars.prefix_color) root.style.setProperty(\"--pc\", vars.prefix_color);\n            if (typeof vars.glitch_a === \"string\" && vars.glitch_a) root.style.setProperty(\"--ga\", vars.glitch_a);\n            if (typeof vars.glitch_b === \"string\" && vars.glitch_b) root.style.setProperty(\"--gb\", vars.glitch_b);\n            lead.textContent = txt(vars.prefix, \"READY TO\");\n            lead.style.display = lead.textContent ? \"\" : \"none\";\n            fillSizer(el(\"wgl-sizer\"), words);\n            var base = num(vars.font_size, 100, 20, 320);\n            function fit() { fitG(g, base, null, 0.88, 0.8); }\n            fit();\n            onFonts(fit);\n\n            // remocn-scenes: during the first 8 frames of every swap (not the last word) the two colour\n            // layers shift by sin(frame * 2) * 5 px in opposite directions.\n            function draw(f) {\n              var ci = Math.min(Math.floor(f / cd), fi);\n              var cT = ci >= fi ? cd : f % cd;\n              var glitching = ci < fi && cT < 8;\n              var gi = glitching ? Math.sin(cT * 2) * 5 : 0;\n              setText(word, words[ci]);\n              setText(la, words[ci]);\n              setText(lb, words[ci]);\n              la.style.display = lb.style.display = glitching ? \"block\" : \"none\";\n              la.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + (gi / 100) + \"em)\";\n              lb.style.transform = \"translateX(\" + (-gi / 100) + \"em)\";\n            }\n            start(draw);\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
